issions that pay once still open per pilot (the tool fleet, view=capacity), what each chain's ask carries, what each gap loads. A one-load gap is flown once by hand (errors.log ENT-027); a draft never lies in the clone (ENT-029). Owed to you by me: the empty-hold check by value, `requires.booked`, the craft step. `requires.booked` is done. For S6: the asks for what the station's list shows without a source in our books (salvage metal, anchor plate, alloy scale, foil scale), and whether a station core or an outpost kit stands on offer anywhere we read. The Crimson Resonance (8,500 cr once, the next link of Signal Fragments, Crimson space 17 to 20 jumps out): Intel read the law (queue.log ENT-089): no bar to a ship without contraband that fires on no one; the risk is 9 unread lawless systems on the way. Step one: one trader that holds Signal Fragments accepts it at Central Nexus with an empty hold and reads whether the accept hands out the titanium alloy (F12). Handed out: one trader flies it as a test, the alloy aboard as the mission's own goods (the one exception to F13's rule of no goods of value out), reading the unread systems on the way, the stance of F2 kept; the route follows its RESULT line. Not handed out: it is not flown (about 6,500 cr of alloy against 8,500 cr, 34 jumps), and you say so in queue.log.
