rds with a route, what each yields an hour and how fast it regrows (the census history), how many hunters that employs, and how many pilots First Hunt still serves in four hours. The railgun ship hunts again when it carries ammunition; the check is owed by me. (6) Carapace: 394 of the fleet's 565 lie in your drones' storage. Six make one armor plate at any workshop, free (Apollo's recipe, guidebook logistics.md), and plate bids stand at four stations in pools of 3 to 6 at 222 to 380 cr: make and sell them where they lie, no more plates than a bid's depth read minutes before; once by hand, then by script (F21). For S6: what stands at the sites Intel names (pilots met, fights seen), from the sight records. From ENT-014: the veil-ray hunts name the curd bid of their sell station (`requires.bid`, 100 cr) and come back on: they open by themselves the hour a docked ship reads the bid back (requests.log ENT-125). Cracking the Shell hunts at GSC-0041 Frost Ring with a herd floor of three (ENT-126). Pirate Bounty stays unflown under F2; it is put to Suggi.
